{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"refractive-hasty-iguanodon","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Observation\nThe `sweep (windows)` job 135597358757 (run 44534782876, main at fa383b1d195, 2026-11-19) failed `tests/unit/test_fixture_env_repr_security.py::test_fixture_failure_does_not_render_unrelated_ambient_secret[tests.scripts.test_observability_exit-healthy_env-None]` at line 71 (`assert result.returncode == 1`). The child pytest session ended with `ERROR collecting test session`: `FileNotFoundError: [WinError 2]` from `Path.lstat()` on `C:\\Users\\runneradmin\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\rebar-ticket-view-534ea34f-s5jdm9m4`. That is a directory in the shared system temp dir, apparently created and then removed by another xdist worker's pinned-ticket-view while the child was enumerating temp. The same test passed in the sweep of run 44526811291 (job 135569438854, main at f8e9ea0e61f) one hour earlier. It is not in any deselect argfile.\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\n1. Something in the child session's collection or fixture setup (for example a repo/temp leak snapshot) lists the system temp dir and lstats each entry, which races concurrent deletions by other workers.\n2. The child inherits the parent's TEMP, so it shares that directory with all xdist workers.\n\n## Next check\nRead the child's full collection traceback (it is truncated in the job log) to find which code enumerates temp. Then either make that enumeration tolerate entries that vanish between listing and lstat, or give the child a private TEMP.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Root cause identified with the frame that enumerates the temp dir.\n- [ ] The enumeration tolerates entries removed concurrently, or the child no longer shares the system temp dir, with a regression test that does not need Windows.\n- [ ] The test passes in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).","id":"3d9f-3788-87f7-45f6","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["windows","flaky-or-platform"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: nested pytest trips on a rebar-ticket-view temp dir removed mid-collection"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795101369415051522,"uuid":"18376653-a0ec-4e73-9dea-d67d098d4f84"}